course: dictionary
lesson: 2929
title: A box that slides in and out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A drawer is a box inside a table, desk or cupboard that slides in and out, for keeping things. «Grandma's best silver spoons come out of the drawer dull and almost black.» The spoons are kept inside the drawer, so the drawer is a container you pull open.
explain: Context can show you which meaning is being used. «When you kick a ball you push it, and when you open a drawer you pull it.» The sentence tells you that a drawer is something you pull, so it must be the box that moves.
explain: Some words belong to a phrase, and the whole phrase has its own meaning. «Not the sharpest knife in the drawer» is a funny way of saying someone is not very clever. You cannot work it out from the word knife alone, so read the whole phrase.
fact: A drawer is a box in a table, desk or cupboard that slides in and out.
fact: «Top drawer» means the very best, and a «chest of drawers» is a piece of furniture with several drawers in it.
fact: Pull drawers gently and only partly, because a heavy drawer can fall out and many open drawers can tip the chest.
fact: Keep sharp knives and medicines in closed drawers, away from small children.
fact: Drawer is spelled like draw with -er on the end, which is why it can also mean a person who draws pictures, but this meaning is rare.
exercise: «Grandma's best silver spoons come out of the drawer dull and almost black.» Where were the spoons kept? | Under the bed | In the bath | On the roof | *In a drawer
exercise: Someone says, «He is not the sharpest knife in the drawer.» What does it mean? | He is the best cook in the house | *He is not very clever | He is very good at cutting | He keeps his knives tidy
exercise: Which phrase means the very best? | Kitchen drawer | *Top drawer | Chest of drawers | Sock drawer
test: Why should you pull a heavy drawer gently and only partly? | Because drawers like to be pushed | Because it makes the drawer squeak less | *Because a heavy drawer can fall out | Because it makes the drawer colder
test: Where should sharp knives and medicines be kept? | On the floor by the door | On the kitchen table | In the bath | *In closed drawers, away from small children
exam: Which meaning of drawer is rare? | *A person who draws pictures | A cupboard door | A piece of furniture with many drawers | A box that slides in and out
